About Time

4
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,639
I always knew my family was a bit weird; I mean, I'm the first one.

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,037
I'm way too lanky, skinny, and my hair is way too orange.

6
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:05,028
My mom was lovely, but she had many traits different from typical moms.

7
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,513
She was a very independent woman.

8
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,672
She was unique, always busy, and quite cool-headed.

9
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,552
Queen was her fashion icon.

10
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:16,917
Dad was more ordinary. He was someone who always had plenty of free time.

11
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:20,316
When he retired from teaching at the university for his 50th birthday,

12
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:23,716
he started chatting with me and even let me win at ping pong,

13
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,637
allowing him to live out the rest of his life in leisure.

14
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:29,238
And there's my mom's brother, Uncle Desmond.

15
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:33,393
My uncle always dresses impeccably. He's always so well-dressed.

16
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:35,078
He doesn't really do much.

17
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:38,073
My uncle was a very charming and intelligent man.

18
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,991
He was always lost in his own thoughts, but we never did find out what they were.

19
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,038
And finally, Catherine.

20
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,839
Katie—or sometimes she goes by KitKat—is my younger sister.

21
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:51,510
Amidst the sensible jackets and haircuts of the family,

22
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:54,194
There's this heavenly child.

23
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:59,115
With fairy-like eyes and her feet always bare, wearing a purple shirt.

24
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,708
She was like that then, and she's still like that now.

25
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:04,553
That kid is the most wonderful being in the world.

26
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:09,478
Overall, it was a happy childhood without anything particularly special happening.

27
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,639
We even drank tea at the beach every day until I turned 21.

28
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,558
Skipping stones and eating sandwiches,

29
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:20,030
Regardless of whether it was summer or winter.

30
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,879
Every Friday night, we watched movies.

31
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,751
No matter the weather.

32
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:34,952
And once a year, there's a terrible New Year's Eve party.

33
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,751
Want another one?

34
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,673
You're really great.

35
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:03,275
I'm Katie. What am I drinking?

36
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,917
This is very expensive.

37
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,394
- Cheers! - Cheers!

38
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,753
It's almost 12 o'clock already.

39
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,831
Let's go, let's go.

40
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,837
I need to find you a girl...

41
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,793
Oh my god!

42
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:34,755
Everyone makes mistakes, it's okay.

43
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:37,998
...6, 5

44
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:41,112
4, 3, 2, 1

45
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:45,512
Happy New Year!

46
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,429
Sorry.

47
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:05,116
The next morning, I woke up hungover, feeling ashamed of myself.

48
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:09,193
Not knowing that this was the day my life would change forever.

49
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,872
Get up, dummy.

50
