164
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:25,997
How is anyone supposed to live their life in this situation?

165
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:30,319
And so time passed without any improvement.

166
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,910
The day came for her to leave.

167
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:35,789
Charlotte, it's our last lunch together.

168
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,148
No way!

169
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:40,790
I really enjoyed spending the summer with you all.

170
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,115
- Right—thank you.

171
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,919
- I had a great time—Right, Desmond?

172
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:49,476
- What? - That you had a great time spending the summer with Charlotte.

173
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,319
Charlotte? Who's Charlotte?

174
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:53,670
Snap out of it, I mean Charlotte, she's sitting right next to you.

175
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,310
- Ah, right, Charlotte—Hi there.

176
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,519
Nice to meet you.

177
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,310
You had a great time spending the summer with Charlotte, right, Team?

178
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:10,949
Yes.

179
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,359
August flew by in an instant.

180
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:15,471
You taught me a lot, didn't you?

181
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,028
Yeah, in a much more sophisticated way.

182
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,873
I'd like to think it was a subtle way.

183
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,073
Come in.

184
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,628
- Charlotte—Yeah.

185
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:47,189
Since tonight is our last night, can I ask you something?

186
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,832
Sure, go ahead.

187
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,479
No, wait a sec.

188
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,912
It's not about love, is it?

189
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,593
Love? Why?

190
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:01,235
KitKat warned me that if you say something like that...

191
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:05,837
...don't treat me like a little sister and act stupid.

192
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,399
He told me to be clear about it.

193
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:11,272
Or did I just make a fool of myself for nothing?

194
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,676
Are you here to ask me the secret to playing good tennis as a final request?

195
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,351
No, it is about love.

196
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,112
Seriously.

197
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,555
How sweet.

198
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:26,676
I regret waiting until the last night.

199
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:31,635
You should have come to my room when we had time.

200
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,795
So "last night" wasn't a good idea?

201
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:39,795
It was a terrible idea; honestly, it's kind of insulting.

202
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,470
There's nothing you can do on "the last night."

203
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:46,112
You're right, I get it.

204
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,913
Come in.

205
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,231
- Hi, Tim. - Charlotte.

206
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:14,312
- Hey. - Have a seat.

207
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,678
I don't know if you noticed,

208
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:23,435
but I've fallen completely for you over the last month.

209
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:27,833
It’s only natural, really.

210
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:32,073
Because you have the face of a goddess

211
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,952
and this hair.

212
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:37,272
But even if your face wasn't pretty,

213
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,953
or even if you were completely bald...

214
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,760
For some medical reason, say.

215
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,156
I still would have adored you.

216
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:48,669
So, I was wondering...

217
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:53,876
I wanted to see if you felt the same way about me.

218
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:56,189
Wow.

219
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:59,397
Let's do this.

220
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:05,956
Why don't we spend the summer together and you can ask me again on our last night?

221
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,637
- The last night? - Yeah.

222
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,993
Let's talk on the last night. We'll see how things go then.

223
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,234
That's interesting.

224
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:17,629
Right.

225
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:22,438
No, that's a perfect plan. Absolutely perfect. The last night.

226
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,993
The last night.

227
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,438
Thanks.

228
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,113
Goodnight, Timmy.

229
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,391
I learned a huge lesson.

230
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:43,711
No matter how much I time travel, I can't make someone love me.

231
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:44,829
Bye!

232
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:48,235
And so, the love of my life departed.

233
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:53,514
And the next day, it was my turn to leave.

234
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:59,272
Here, don't use it all at once.

235
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,949
Thank you.

236
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:07,393
Don't call too often; your mom hates being disturbed.

237
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,670
Got it, thanks.

238
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:32,471
I boarded a train to London to find Mira and her woman.

239
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:37,395
I ended up living in St. John's Wood near Abbey Road

240
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:40,631
with Harry, a playwright friend of my father's.

241
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:44,674
When going somewhere new, having a connection always helps.

242
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:01,354
Who the hell are you?

243
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,989
- I'm James's son. - Who?

244
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,316
- James Lake. - What's that supposed to mean?

245
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,752
I heard you were renting out a room.

246
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,594
Go inside and wait.

247
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,910
Quietly. Don't make a sound.

248
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,432
Or I'll kill you.

249
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,554
When you rang the doorbell, for the first time in ten years,

250
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,198
I actually had a good idea.

251
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,632
But now I've forgotten it.

252
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,356
You damn brat.

253
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,072
How's your dad?

254
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:50,478
I always thought he was a weird guy. Your dad has something suspicious about him.

255
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:53,956
- Really? - Yeah, honestly, I didn't even like him.

256
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,514
Does your mom still look like Andy Warhol?

257
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:58,629
What did you say?

258
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,594
This is my wife.

259
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:05,752
- She's beautiful. - Yeah, she doesn't give off a great first impression.

260
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,991
She's incredibly sarcastic.

261
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,270
But as you live with her,

262
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:15,433
you realize she's the coolest woman in the world.

263
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:18,430
So she probably left you.

264
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,558
Right here.

265
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:26,954
Don't be too loud, especially when you're having sex.

266
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,635
There won't be any opportunities for that.

267
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:31,439
Dammit, two idiots living under one roof.

268
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,791
This is my daughter.

269
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:38,795
Sex with her if you want; I doubt there's a man who hasn't.

270
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,548
It wasn't an environment where one could dream of romance.

271
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:46,959
It was the same at work.

272
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:50,119
The legal world seems to be full of men.

273
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:56,632
Hi, I'm Lori. Nice to meet you. Really nice to meet you.

274
00:19:57,120 --> 00:20:00,749
Who knows, maybe we'll become best friends.

