I see you've met Aunt May.

1109
01:15:27,200 --> 01:15:30,988
Goodness, everyone should at least wear name tags.

1110
01:15:32,120 --> 01:15:34,190
Next time it's your turn, Kittle Cattle.

1111
01:15:35,440 --> 01:15:37,431
I don't know, Uncle D.

1112
01:15:39,280 --> 01:15:41,157
Men are mean.

1113
01:15:41,720 --> 01:15:43,278
Aren't they?

1114
01:15:43,800 --> 01:15:45,677
In my experience, they are.

1115
01:15:46,800 --> 01:15:50,998
They always try to enjoy their freedom without paying the price.

1116
01:15:54,840 --> 01:15:56,398


1117
01:15:56,520 --> 01:15:58,636
I'm glad you think so.

1118
01:16:06,480 --> 01:16:09,631
Should we have wished for less rain?

1119
01:16:09,720 --> 01:16:10,709
No.

1120
01:16:11,800 --> 01:16:13,677
It was perfect.

1121
01:16:14,880 --> 01:16:15,869
*Sigh*

1122
01:16:18,880 --> 01:16:21,189
Now it begins.

1123
01:16:21,680 --> 01:16:24,592
There will be many more days.

1124
01:16:25,480 --> 01:16:26,469
It's fun!

1125
01:16:33,000 --> 01:16:33,989
Forge

1126
01:16:35,640 --> 01:16:37,358
It's Forge's.

1127
01:16:37,960 --> 01:16:40,155
The prettiest girl in the world

1128
01:16:43,560 --> 01:16:47,553
You want to go to your dad, I know

1129
01:16:50,840 --> 01:16:51,829
Right

1130
01:16:54,920 --> 01:16:58,515
No one can prepare you for having a child.

1131
01:16:58,680 --> 01:17:02,992
The moment I held my baby in my arms, I realized they were my responsibility now.

1132
01:17:03,920 --> 01:17:07,754
No one can prepare you for love and fear.

1133
01:17:09,360 --> 01:17:11,316
You're so lovely.

1134
01:17:12,360 --> 01:17:14,351
You were such an ugly little baby.

1135
01:17:14,720 --> 01:17:16,392
You were more like a chimpanzee than a human.

1136
01:17:17,040 --> 01:17:18,553
I still remember the first time I saw you.

1137
01:17:18,640 --> 01:17:21,552
I was just glad we didn't live near the London Zoo.

1138
01:17:22,760 --> 01:17:25,832
Let's see, give me the baby. Let's see if he/she is fussing.

1139
01:17:25,920 --> 01:17:27,717
- Still... - Of course they're fussing.

1140
01:17:27,880 --> 01:17:30,269
- Look at this - They can do anything.

1141
01:17:30,400 --> 01:17:32,356
- Look - Hi there.

1142
01:17:34,560 --> 01:17:36,039
Oh, my little one.

1143
01:17:37,080 --> 01:17:40,675
I can't compare my love for those who love me...

1144
01:17:42,920 --> 01:17:44,319
...to the indifference of a friend without children.

1145
01:17:44,400 --> 01:17:46,356
There's nothing to compare it to.

1146
01:17:46,440 --> 01:17:50,228
- Should we go to Uncle Jay's? - No, never mind. It's fine.

1147
01:17:50,600 --> 01:17:52,795
The moment you have to move into a place you can barely afford

1148
01:17:52,880 --> 01:17:55,713
comes around so fast it's shocking.

1149
01:17:56,280 --> 01:17:59,272
- Look what I found! - Look who it is!

1150
01:17:59,880 --> 01:18:02,189
- Tim! - Sorry.

1151
01:18:04,920 --> 01:18:08,595
Suddenly, time travel felt unnecessary.

1152
01:18:08,720 --> 01:18:10,756
Because every single moment of my life had been so wonderful.

1153
01:18:10,920 --> 01:18:13,388
"Happy birthday, Pozzy."

1154
01:18:18,280 --> 01:18:19,713
What's your name?

1155
01:18:19,840 --> 01:18:22,229
- I think Horace sounds good. - Yeah, I like that.

1156
01:18:22,320 --> 01:18:24,515
I heard that as a godfather, the most important thing

1157
01:18:24,600 --> 01:18:26,955
is that you should never give a gift smaller than the child.

1158
01:18:27,120 --> 01:18:29,429
Shut up, you jerk.

1159
01:18:29,560 --> 01:18:33,519
Don't worry, I didn't bring any gifts anyway. You don't know that because you don't have a brain.

1160
01:18:33,640 --> 01:18:37,792
I didn't expect you to come here; this isn't really Harry Potter style.

1161
01:18:37,960 --> 01:18:41,111
Right, Mary. I was scammed. I only came because they said there'd be free booze.

1162
01:18:43,000 --> 01:18:45,116
As you know, I hate kids.

1163
01:18:45,320 --> 01:18:46,912
But where's KitKat?

1164
01:18:47,280 --> 01:18:50,272
I'm not sure. They said she'd be here around 3:00.

1165
01:18:50,360 --> 01:18:53,670
And I even made special purple cupcakes for her.

1166
01:18:54,160 --> 01:18:57,072
- She's here! - They say if you talk about a tiger, it shows up.

1167
01:18:58,800 --> 01:19:01,314
Let's wait until Auntie KitKat gets here.

1168
01:19:02,320 --> 01:19:03,833
- Hello. - Jimmy.

1169
01:19:04,000 --> 01:19:05,479
Where's my brother?

1170
01:19:06,840 --> 01:19:08,990
- I thought he was already here. - No, he hasn't shown up yet.

1171
01:19:10,880 --> 01:19:12,393
That sucks.

1172
01:19:12,920 --> 01:19:14,592
What do you mean?

1173
01:19:16,000 --> 01:19:20,596
We had a bit of a fight this morning over nothing, and then we drank...

1174
01:19:21,520 --> 01:19:25,035
I drove all the way here thinking you'd come.

1175
01:19:25,160 --> 01:19:27,549
I told you we should meet here...

1176
01:19:27,920 --> 01:19:31,356
There's a song by Buzz Lowman called "Sunscreen."

1177
01:19:31,520 --> 01:19:33,670
He said worrying about the future

1178
01:19:33,760 --> 01:19:38,038
Is as useless as trying to solve an equation by blowing bubbles with gum.

1179
01:19:38,680 --> 01:19:40,750
The truly serious problems in life

1180
01:19:40,920 --> 01:19:44,674
Are always things we haven't even thought of yet.

1181
01:19:58,240 --> 01:19:59,389
What happened?

1182
01:20:01,200 --> 01:20:02,872
We fought.

1183
01:20:03,400 --> 01:20:04,389
And...

1184
01:20:05,720 --> 01:20:08,234
I think I might be a bit drunk.

1185
01:20:10,040 --> 01:20:11,917
- How is it? - Not good.

1186
01:20:12,240 --> 01:20:16,756
When did you leave? Where were you? Give me the exact time and address.

1187
01:20:26,560 --> 01:20:29,120
We're here. Sorry, sorry.

1188
01:20:29,400 --> 01:20:30,628
Come in.

1189
01:20:31,680 --> 01:20:33,238
Oh my god.

1190
01:20:33,560 --> 01:20:35,596
- Hi. - I brought them.

1191
01:20:35,920 --> 01:20:37,911
Does a little baby live here?

1192
01:20:38,080 --> 01:20:42,232
Yes, they're very excited. They're downstairs.

1193
01:20:42,840 --> 01:20:44,910
Happy birthday, Posey.

1194
01:20:47,120 --> 01:20:49,680
Sorry, I had to bring KitKat.

1195
01:20:49,800 --> 01:20:53,509
- I thought you were driving yourself. - That's how it turned out.

1196
01:20:54,760 --> 01:20:56,876
- Are you okay? - I'll tell you later.

1197
01:20:59,240 --> 01:21:01,196
I'm worried about KitKat.

1198
01:21:03,200 --> 01:21:05,191
Yeah, I know.

1199
01:21:05,880 --> 01:21:08,872
She kept drinking wine while we were having tea.

1200
01:21:09,480 --> 01:21:11,914
Jimmy was being mean,

1201
01:21:12,040 --> 01:21:15,112
And she wouldn't even have a purple cupcake.

1202
01:21:15,920 --> 01:21:18,229
I have to fix this somehow.

1203
01:21:20,400 --> 01:21:21,389
Right.

1204
01:21:22,400 --> 01:21:24,072
But...

1205
01:21:24,800 --> 01:21:29,032
Someone has to want to change for something to get fixed.

1206
01:21:30,480 --> 01:21:31,469
Maybe so.

1207
01:21:32,520 --> 01:21:33,999
Or maybe not.

1208
01:21:37,960 --> 01:21:40,235
What happened?

1209
01:21:40,560 --> 01:21:45,315
You're the coolest person in the world. Just as amazing as my wife.

1210
01:21:47,040 --> 01:21:48,996
Maybe...

1211
01:21:50,120 --> 01:21:51,872
I'm just a burden.

1212
01:21:52,760 --> 01:21:56,469
Every family has someone like that.

1213
01:21:56,840 --> 01:21:59,798
Bad grades, ruins everything they do...

1214
01:21:59,920 --> 01:22:01,911
Someone whose life is a mess.

1215
01:22:02,440 --> 01:22:04,556
I guess I'm the black sheep of our family.

1216
01:22:05,680 --> 01:22:06,669
No.

1217
01:22:07,720 --> 01:22:08,869
That's not true.

1218
01:22:15,960 --> 01:22:18,952
Okay, I'll tell you the secret.

1219
01:22:19,120 --> 01:22:21,350
You have to promise to keep it.

1220
01:22:21,640 --> 01:22:24,518
- We always keep each other's secrets. - Did we?

1221
01:22:24,960 --> 01:22:27,599
Never, ever, ever, ever.

1222
01:22:27,760 --> 01:22:30,035
Ever, ever, ever, ever, ever.

1223
01:22:30,640 --> 01:22:33,313
Do you promise never to tell?

1224
01:22:33,600 --> 01:22:34,589
Yeah.

1225
01:22:40,320 --> 01:22:42,754
I can travel through time.

1226
01:22:45,840 --> 01:22:48,115
Why are you standing inside the cupboard under the stairs?

1227
01:22:48,240 --> 01:22:51,676
Because you have to act differently when you go back in time.

1228
01:22:51,800 --> 01:22:53,677
You're so funny when you're like this.

1229
01:22:53,800 --> 01:22:56,030
Hold my hand and close your eyes tight.

1230
01:23:13,080 --> 01:23:16,470
Oh my god! Oh my god!

1231
01:23:17,200 --> 01:23:21,034
This is unbelievable!

1232
01:23:25,960 --> 01:23:26,995
Are you kidding me?

1233
01:23:27,080 --> 01:23:30,789
You could go back anytime, but you brought me to the worst party of my life?

1234
01:23:30,920 --> 01:23:32,990
Sorry, let's go.

1235
01:23:35,920 --> 01:23:38,150
- I have stuff to do. - What stuff?

1236
01:23:38,320 --> 01:23:41,312
You're not seeing Jimmy Kincaid.

1237
01:23:41,440 --> 01:23:42,839
Hurry, get inside.

1238
01:23:44,760 --> 01:23:48,116
- But I was just about to fall for you! - Not this time.

1239
01:23:57,880 --> 01:24:01,190
Who's the prettiest? Jennifer, right?

1240
01:24:01,320 --> 01:24:03,834
- Yeah. - She's gorgeous!

1241
01:24:03,960 --> 01:24:06,758
- I love your skirt, Jennifer. - Thanks.

1242
01:24:06,880 --> 01:24:09,314
Right, okay.

1243
01:24:09,480 --> 01:24:13,553
You mean even if it wasn't me, you would've slept with someone else?

1244
01:24:13,960 --> 01:24:15,871
It's in the past.

1245
01:24:18,880 --> 01:24:20,552
Wait a second, Jimmy.

1246
01:24:21,640 --> 01:24:23,551
- Sorry. - Do I know you?

1247
01:24:23,680 --> 01:24:25,511
Of course.

1248
01:24:26,120 --> 01:24:28,759
I know you very well. Sorry.

1249
01:24:28,880 --> 01:24:31,269
This should have happened from the start.

1250
01:24:37,320 --> 01:24:40,471
Happy New Year, everyone. Happy New Year.

1251
01:24:40,600 --> 01:24:42,511
Get back to the pantry, quick.

1252
01:24:45,040 --> 01:24:46,189
Awesome!

1253
01:24:46,480 --> 01:24:49,199
- So, what happens now? - Only God knows.

1254
01:24:49,320 --> 01:24:50,912
All I want is from this moment on...

1255
01:24:51,000 --> 01:24:53,992
For you not to meet any disgusting, bad guys. Because they're disgusting and bad.

1256
01:24:54,400 --> 01:24:56,755
Since when did you get so serious?

1257
01:24:56,880 --> 01:24:59,189
From the moment I realized I might lose you.

1258
01:25:01,960 --> 01:25:04,679
Brace yourself, it might be weird.

1259
01:25:05,240 --> 01:25:07,196
Things might have changed.

1260
01:25:13,560 --> 01:25:14,913
Oh my god.

1261
01:25:15,040 --> 01:25:17,235
- Why? - Jay.

1262
01:25:17,360 --> 01:25:19,157
- That Jay? - Yeah.

1263
01:25:19,840 --> 01:25:23,196
He's so cute, oh my god.

1264
01:25:24,800 --> 01:25:25,789
Yeah.

1265
01:25:26,400 --> 01:25:27,913
Let's go out.

1266
01:25:33,880 --> 01:25:35,393
Welcome home.

1267
01:25:36,040 --> 01:25:39,077
Mom is planning something new.

1268
01:25:44,400 --> 01:25:46,994
I have something in mind.

1269
01:25:47,120 --> 01:25:49,839
- I know what she's going to say. - Go grab a snack and then help me.

1270
01:25:51,440 --> 01:25:53,749
Leave the rest to Uncle D.

1271
01:25:56,240 --> 01:25:58,515
Just tidy things up.

1272
01:25:58,920 --> 01:26:00,911
- Are you okay? I missed you. - Yeah.

1273
01:26:01,440 --> 01:26:04,079
- Your mom asked for help with the garden. - Okay.

1274
01:26:06,280 --> 01:26:11,070
Just tidy it up; just pull out the dead ones since it's a mess.

1275
01:26:11,240 --> 01:26:14,073
It's exactly how we wanted it, right?

1276
01:26:14,240 --> 01:26:15,593
- The dead ones. - Look at this.

1277
01:26:18,280 --> 01:26:20,714
It's a total mess because of the bugs.

1278
01:26:33,640 --> 01:26:37,315
- What happened? - It's completely satisfying.

1279
01:26:37,720 --> 01:26:41,235
That's great. Tell me more.

1280
01:26:41,320 --> 01:26:43,311
Can you help me prepare dinner?

1281
01:26:43,400 --> 01:26:45,277
If I don't finish by 6 o'clock, I'm gonna get fired.

1282
01:26:45,440 --> 01:26:48,750
Yeah, it's exactly what I want to do.

1283
01:26:48,880 --> 01:26:51,952
Let's see, where is the coolest person in the world?

1284
01:26:52,120 --> 01:26:56,955
Come to Dad and I'll give you some yummy treats.

1285
01:27:04,080 --> 01:27:05,559
Hi, baby.

1286
01:27:09,480 --> 01:27:10,913
You, wait a sec.

1287
01:27:11,040 --> 01:27:13,474
Stay here, I'll be right back.

1288
01:27:25,840 --> 01:27:27,751
Dad, can we talk for a minute?

1289
01:27:27,840 --> 01:27:29,671
Sure.

1290
01:27:31,680 --> 01:27:35,389
- Can't we go back before the birth? - No, I didn't say that.

1291
01:27:35,520 --> 01:27:40,674
It's fine until birth, but since the exact sperm and the exact moment...

1292
01:27:40,840 --> 01:27:42,068
...created this child,

1293
01:27:42,160 --> 01:27:45,789
Even a slight difference would result in a different child.

1294
01:27:47,920 --> 01:27:52,596
Then everything up until yesterday was all the same? Does it mean we lose everything?

1295
01:27:53,520 --> 01:27:55,795
It's the same as with other people.

1296
01:27:55,960 --> 01:27:57,837
I see, that's interesting.

1297
01:27:58,640 --> 01:28:01,313
That's a headache. I love you, Dad, I have to go.

1298
01:28:25,720 --> 01:28:27,631
- Go home. - No.

1299
01:28:27,720 --> 01:28:29,312
Until I find a way to make sure this never happens again,

1300
01:28:29,400 --> 01:28:33,188
I'm staying here.

1301
01:28:46,040 --> 01:28:47,712
Can you leave now?

1302
01:29:01,040 --> 01:29:03,429
I should break up with Jimmy, right?

1303
01:29:04,440 --> 01:29:05,919
Forever.

1304
01:29:06,880 --> 01:29:08,074
And...

1305
01:29:08,240 --> 01:29:10,276
I have to quit drinking too.

1306
01:29:13,200 --> 01:29:15,077
Stop quitting my job.

1307
01:29:17,120 --> 01:29:21,193
And date someone else.

1308
01:29:21,920 --> 01:29:24,593
Someone nice and boring.

1309
01:29:27,600 --> 01:29:28,794
Right

1310
01:29:32,120 --> 01:29:35,237


1311
01:29:35,360 --> 01:29:36,634


1312
01:29:37,760 --> 01:29:39,239


1313
01:29:39,640 --> 01:29:40,959


1314
01:29:41,960 --> 01:29:43,552


1315
01:29:43,640 --> 01:29:46,871


1316
01:29:46,960 --> 01:29:51,476


1317
01:29:51,600 --> 01:29:52,589


1318
01:29:53,440 --> 01:29:56,398


1319
01:29:56,760 --> 01:29:58,751


1320
01:30:00,440 --> 01:30:01,589


1321
01:30:01,720 --> 01:30:04,109


1322
01:30:04,240 --> 01:30:07,994


1323
01:30:08,120 --> 01:30:10,350


1324
01:30:17,040 --> 01:30:19,952


1325
01:30:20,080 --> 01:30:23,436


1326
01:30:23,600 --> 01:30:26,717


1327
01:30:27,000 --> 01:30:28,513
Where's Posey?

1328
01:30:29,200 --> 01:30:31,668
Over there! Hi!

1329
01:30:31,800 --> 01:30:34,519
Hi! Hi.

1330
01:30:34,640 --> 01:30:36,835
How's our little baby doing?

1331
01:30:40,440 --> 01:30:42,351
Let's have another one.

1332
01:30:44,160 --> 01:30:47,197
No way, I hate that.

1333
01:30:49,080 --> 01:30:52,072
It hurts, and I'm seriously getting so fat.

1334
01:30:52,200 --> 01:30:54,475
You did get a bit chubby.

1335
01:30:54,840 --> 01:30:56,796
Tell Mom we need a sister.

1336
01:30:56,920 --> 01:31:00,993
No, tell Dad I want to be an only child.

1337
01:31:02,760 --> 01:31:07,675
Luckily, we were young and reckless, so soon enough, you became a family of four.

1338
01:31:07,800 --> 01:31:11,156
Absolutely brilliant. Posey Lake, Bangnyeong III.

1339
01:31:11,280 --> 01:31:14,272
She's about to break the women's 10-meter Olympic record.

1340
01:31:14,400 --> 01:31:18,518
She'll do it—she did it! That was amazing.

1341
01:31:18,640 --> 01:31:21,359
Truly incredible. You did great.

1342
01:31:21,480 --> 01:31:22,879
He sleeps well even with all this noise.

1343
01:31:23,000 --> 01:31:25,275
Can you help me? I'm dying of nerves here.

1344
01:31:25,360 --> 01:31:27,669
What should I wear for dinner with our best-selling author?

1345
01:31:27,800 --> 01:31:30,360
We'll feed the rascals and head up in a bit.

1346
01:31:30,480 --> 01:31:31,674
Okay, thanks.

1347
01:31:32,040 --> 01:31:33,439
Try again.

1348
01:31:33,880 --> 01:31:36,474
Okay, how about this one?

1349
01:31:36,600 --> 01:31:39,114
Nice, good choice. I like it.

1350
01:31:39,240 --> 01:31:42,391
No, look closely at this...

1351
01:31:43,040 --> 01:31:46,032
I don't know, I hate it. I don't like it.

1352
01:31:46,360 --> 01:31:48,078
- Yeah - It's too boring.

1353
01:31:48,600 --> 01:31:51,478
And I look a bit fat.

1354
01:31:51,600 --> 01:31:54,398
Right, it's boring and makes me look fat. I hate it too.

1355
01:31:56,280 --> 01:31:58,111
Okay, how about this one?

1356
01:31:58,520 --> 01:32:00,476
Gorgeous. That's the one.

1357
01:32:00,960 --> 01:32:03,235
No, the neckline is too low.

1358
01:32:03,360 --> 01:32:04,349
Really?

1359
01:32:04,440 --> 01:32:06,476
- I like it - This one isn't as low.

1360
01:32:06,600 --> 01:32:09,672
No, I can't wear these shoes. They make me look like a hooker.

1361
01:32:09,800 --> 01:32:13,156
- Then just take off the heels - Then I'll look completely flat.

1362
01:32:13,280 --> 01:32:15,794
You'd rather look like a hooker or a dwarf?

1363
01:32:16,920 --> 01:32:19,036
Warning, I'm warning you.

1364
01:32:22,720 --> 01:32:23,755
Fine!

1365
01:32:23,880 --> 01:32:24,869
No.

1366
01:32:28,800 --> 01:32:29,789
Stop it!

1367
01:32:30,840 --> 01:32:32,910
I like that one.

1368
01:32:33,200 --> 01:32:38,320
This is the underwear to go under the dress, dummy.

1369
01:32:40,720 --> 01:32:42,995
- This one? - Not bad.

1370
01:32:43,640 --> 01:32:46,473
- Or this? - You're just testing them out, right? They're the same.

1371
01:32:46,600 --> 01:32:47,589
No!

1372
