Hi, Mom.

1413
01:34:45,840 --> 01:34:47,831
No, it's okay, we're...

1414
01:34:48,040 --> 01:34:49,792
I'll be down shortly.

1415
01:34:50,680 --> 01:34:51,999
Yes.

1416
01:35:06,600 --> 01:35:09,433
- You're here. - Mom, how are you feeling?

1417
01:35:10,520 --> 01:35:12,795
- Honestly? - Be honest.

1418
01:35:13,200 --> 01:35:15,873
I'm furious.

1419
01:35:16,520 --> 01:35:21,150
You really don't care about a life without your father, do you?

1420
01:35:22,400 --> 01:35:24,630
Mary, come here. Let me give you some tea.

1421
01:35:25,520 --> 01:35:27,875
- How are you? - I'm okay.

1422
01:35:28,000 --> 01:35:30,389
- Did you eat anything? - Yes.

1423
01:35:36,440 --> 01:35:37,475
Uncle.

1424
01:35:38,880 --> 01:35:41,553
- How are you feeling? - I'm okay, thank you.

1425
01:35:42,000 --> 01:35:43,638
It's a bit hot, though.

1426
01:35:47,840 --> 01:35:50,479
I don't think your dad is doing well.

1427
01:35:51,480 --> 01:35:52,595
It's cancer.

1428
01:35:53,840 --> 01:35:54,829
Yes.

1429
01:35:55,280 --> 01:35:57,794
This is really upsetting, Tim.

1430
01:35:59,800 --> 01:36:01,791
Didn't your dad say he loved me at your wedding?

1431
01:36:02,280 --> 01:36:04,316
- Because he loves her. - I know.

1432
01:36:06,280 --> 01:36:08,589
That day was the best day of my life.

1433
01:36:11,200 --> 01:36:13,509
So today must be the worst day.

1434
01:36:19,760 --> 01:36:20,749
Dad.

1435
01:36:23,040 --> 01:36:24,951
My god.

1436
01:36:25,480 --> 01:36:27,311
Don't you start acting like that too.

1437
01:36:27,440 --> 01:36:28,475
Like what?

1438
01:36:28,560 --> 01:36:32,348
KitKat just burst into tears and left, and now you're doing it too.

1439
01:36:32,440 --> 01:36:33,919
Whatever did Mom say?

1440
01:36:34,120 --> 01:36:36,315
- Just the truth. - Okay.

1441
01:36:37,520 --> 01:36:39,158
That aside...

1442
01:36:40,080 --> 01:36:45,677
I think it was because of the smoking, but since it was before you were born, there was no choice.

1443
01:36:46,400 --> 01:36:48,789
Even so, if it wasn't for my sexy way of smoking...

1444
01:36:48,880 --> 01:36:51,348
Your mom wouldn't have fallen for me.

1445
01:36:54,440 --> 01:36:58,558
We got the diagnosis as fast as possible, but it was already too late.

1446
01:37:00,440 --> 01:37:03,159
- How much time is left? - Who knows.

1447
01:37:03,280 --> 01:37:05,475
That's the thing.

1448
01:37:05,600 --> 01:37:07,079
It could be years.

1449
01:37:09,880 --> 01:37:11,552
Seriously, how much time is left?

1450
01:37:14,240 --> 01:37:15,878
I'm sorry, but it's about a few weeks.

1451
01:37:23,360 --> 01:37:25,874
Have we had this conversation before?

1452
01:37:28,760 --> 01:37:29,749
Yeah.

1453
01:37:31,520 --> 01:37:33,238
What happened?

1454
01:37:33,360 --> 01:37:35,874
I made a scene.

1455
01:37:36,320 --> 01:37:37,958
I hugged you.

1456
01:37:57,360 --> 01:38:01,035
- Sorry. - If we use time travel...

1457
01:38:01,680 --> 01:38:06,037
No, you didn't say we could fix anything with that.

1458
01:38:06,160 --> 01:38:08,674
Life is unpredictable, no matter whose life it is.

1459
01:38:08,800 --> 01:38:12,793
Look at Jesus. He was the Son of God, and look what happened to him.

1460
01:38:12,920 --> 01:38:14,148
I know, but...

1461
01:38:15,120 --> 01:38:17,588
I feel betrayed somehow.

1462
01:38:17,720 --> 01:38:22,748
Don't say that. Think of it the other way: the only person who wants to play table tennis more often with their son is a time traveler with cancer who can retire at fifty.

1463
01:38:22,880 --> 01:38:27,556
I see.

1464
01:38:29,680 --> 01:38:30,669
Is that why?

1465
01:38:32,480 --> 01:38:34,471
I'm sorry I have to call you like this; things took a turn for the worse suddenly.

1466
01:38:36,840 --> 01:38:40,469
I have something important to tell you. First, let me ask you this.

1467
01:38:46,280 --> 01:38:51,354
Do you want to know the big secret?

1468
01:38:51,680 --> 01:38:54,319
Or would you rather find out on your own like I did?

1469
01:38:54,400 --> 01:38:56,675
Are you saying there's another secret?

1470
01:38:56,800 --> 01:38:58,836
It's not as dramatic as last time, but it's much more important.

1471
01:38:59,680 --> 01:39:02,831
Wow, seriously.

1472
01:39:03,600 --> 01:39:06,273
Please tell me.

1473
01:39:08,840 --> 01:39:11,354
Since saving time is better...

1474
01:39:11,680 --> 01:39:13,636
And then he told me his formula for happiness.

1475
01:39:18,880 --> 01:39:22,509
The first of two steps is to live an ordinary life.

1476
01:39:24,560 --> 01:39:28,792
Living every day just like everyone else.

1477
01:39:28,880 --> 01:39:31,872
The current status is highlighted in this draft.

1478
